<title>FRANCE: January household sentiment index rises.</title>
<headline>January household sentiment index rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>INSEE gave the following data on household opinions. A positive figure shows the percentage points by which the percentage of respondents saying things had improved or risen outnumbered the percentage saying the opposite.</p>
<p>				    Jan  Dec  Nov  Oct  Sept Jul  Jun</p>
<p> Overall Index		  -30  -33  -34  -34  -36  -35  -36</p>
<p> Future living standards    -34  -38  -39  -39  -44  -43  -43</p>
<p> Future unemployment	   61   54   66   70   76   76   59</p>
<p> Past inflation		 -42  -53  -53  -52  -54  -47  -42</p>
<p> Future inflation	     -33  -37  -34  -36  -37  -44  -40</p>
<p> Good time to spend	   -23  -25  -29  -31  -34  -32  -32</p>
<p> Good time to save	     52   51   54   54   53   50   56</p>
<p> Current personal finances   10    9    9    6    9    9   10</p>
<p> Past personal finances     -20  -21  -22  -23  -23  -23  -25</p>
<p> Future personal finances    -6   -8   -8   -8  -10  -10  -10</p>
<p> Ability to save		-30  -29  -27  -29  -31  -30  -29</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
